    {
      "proposal_id": "CS-PROP-JCM1430_FERROUS_SULFATE_HCL_STOCK",
      "old_path": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/concentration_stocks/proposals/JCM1430_Ferrous_Sulfate_HCl_Stock.yaml",
      "old_sha256": "6e0ae3d8ec0984d7e29034b2fd41d3589f26fb7f236bdcc7a829d632837e0c59",
      "new_path": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/successor-1226-1237-v1/payloads/CS-PROP-JCM1430_FERROUS_SULFATE_HCL_STOCK.yaml",
      "new_sha256": "9ce46ee43a275add8f13d2fcabe353f15829654b6f623cdf4fae26dcf717517a",
      "typing_entry_count": 1,
      "science_scope": true,
      "unchanged_bytes": false,
      "science_deltas_separate_from_typing_and_event": [
        {
          "path": "notes",
          "old": "JCM1430 and1431 explicitly give0.01MFeSO4·7H2O in0.02NHCl; stock is added3mL aftercoolingto50C. Normality is preserved and no unsupported1Mconversionorfinaldoseconcentration inferred. Exactsourcecarrier defines thisstock withoutclaiming solidFeSO4identity. Source occurrence IDs and receiving doses remain in the campaign ledger/CultureMech; no complete medium is asserted as thisstock. New0/0statsmeanmembershipnotyetrefreshed,notobservedabsence.",
          "new": "JCM1430 and1431 explicitly give0.01MFeSO4·7H2O in0.02NHCl; stock is added3mL aftercoolingto50C. Normality is preserved and no unsupported1Mconversionorfinaldoseconcentration inferred. Exactsourcecarrier defines thisstock withoutclaiming solidFeSO4identity. Source occurrence IDs and receiving doses remain in the campaign ledger/CultureMech; no complete medium is asserted as thisstock. New0/0statsmeanmembershipnotyetrefreshed,notobservedabsence. MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 / CHEM-COMP-006 (#1237): the complete raw label '0.01 M FeSO4·7H2O solution (in 0.02 N HCl)' is an identity-bearing name for this operational stock: it states the ferrous sulfate heptahydrate reagent, 0.01 M strength, and 0.02 N HCl carrier. JCM1430 and JCM1431 print that name and a 3.0 mL receiving dose after cooling to 50 C. Its former blanket REJECTED_LABEL disposition is superseded by EXACT_SYNONYM; the exact old rejection text, source and prior history are retained in science/qualifier-negative-audit-lineage-v1.json and the immutable predecessor. No competing preferred owner was found for the complete token in the explicitly checked current mapped directory and worker01 selected proposals, so owned-name SUPPRESS is not warranted in that scope. This change does not make shortened ferrous sulfate names equivalent to the stock, infer molecular speciation, or alter component grounding."
        },
        {
          "path": "synonyms[0].source",
          "old": "Exact source-context label from https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1430; unqualified/cross-reference spelling is retained for provenance only and requires the bound source occurrence to resolve.",
          "new": "JCM1430 https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1430 and JCM1431 https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1431, complete stock label in post-cooling additions. CHEM-COMP-006 (#1237) individual reassessment; original rejected assertion/source preserved in immutable predecessor and science/qualifier-negative-audit-lineage-v1.json."
        },
        {
          "path": "synonyms[0].synonym_type",
          "old": "REJECTED_LABEL",
          "new": "EXACT_SYNONYM"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK",
      "old_path": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/concentration_stocks/proposals/NBRC1321_CO2_Bicarbonate_Stock-v2.yaml",
      "old_sha256": "61c0a226a8a99d96b43657f6e00075e901ce051a698b01bd99f6ab6f1d88717c",
      "new_path": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/successor-1226-1237-v1/payloads/CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK.yaml",
      "new_sha256": "f7aca68cf65299a813290c8831a568126f3f18eb4ecf50dec60c8f178246a61a",
      "typing_entry_count": 2,
      "science_scope": true,
      "unchanged_bytes": false,
      "science_deltas_separate_from_typing_and_event": [
        {
          "path": "notes",
          "old": "This exact source preparation uses8.4gNaHCO3 with100mLwater,CO2saturation andsealedautoclaving. The original amount iswateradded,notanexplicitmake-uptofinal100mL. Generic84g/Lstock owner and its J451autoclavedunderCO2context do not establish identical finalvolume or priorCO2saturation. A distinct source-defined operational identity preserves these facts rather than silentlymergingbyrounded1Mmolarity. Source occurrence IDs and receiving doses remain in the campaign ledger/CultureMech; no complete medium is asserted as thisstock. New0/0statsmeanmembershipnotyetrefreshed,notobservedabsence. Cross-lane deduplication: NBRC1257 and NBRC1321 both specify 8.4 g NaHCO3 plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation and autoclaving in tightly sealed CO2-filled bottles. The source qualification and complete preparation establish the same stock; neither source states make-up to a final 100 mL.",
          "new": "This exact source preparation uses8.4gNaHCO3 with100mLwater,CO2saturation andsealedautoclaving. The original amount iswateradded,notanexplicitmake-uptofinal100mL. Generic84g/Lstock owner and its J451autoclavedunderCO2context do not establish identical finalvolume or priorCO2saturation. A distinct source-defined operational identity preserves these facts rather than silentlymergingbyrounded1Mmolarity. Source occurrence IDs and receiving doses remain in the campaign ledger/CultureMech; no complete medium is asserted as thisstock. New0/0statsmeanmembershipnotyetrefreshed,notobservedabsence. Cross-lane deduplication: NBRC1257 and NBRC1321 both specify 8.4 g NaHCO3 plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation and autoclaving in tightly sealed CO2-filled bottles. The source qualification and complete preparation establish the same stock; neither source states make-up to a final 100 mL. 'Bicarbonate solution (1.0 M)***': NBRC1321 uses this exact string as the receiving-table pointer to its *** footnote. The text gives a nominal strength but does not name the sodium salt, added-water recipe, or CO2 saturation that defines this proposed preparation. The *** footnote supplies NaHCO3 8.4 g plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation, and autoclaving in tightly sealed CO2-filled bottles. It is a valid source pointer and broader material description, but is not an identity-bearing standalone name for this particular CO2-conditioned stock. Retain the original sourced REJECTED_LABEL entry and resolve only the explicitly bound source occurrence, rather than claim exact identity for that token outside its footnote.MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 / CHEM-COMP-006 (#1237), individual label assessments:  'Bicarbonate solution***': NBRC1257 uses this exact string as its receiving-table *** pointer, without even the nominal strength. Its *** footnote positively specifies the same NaHCO3 8.4 g plus 100 mL distilled water and CO2 saturation/sealed autoclaving as NBRC1321. The bare token does not identify that sodium/quantity/CO2 preparation independently of the footnote. Retain its exact sourced REJECTED_LABEL entry as a non-name for this specific owner, while retaining the positive source-occurrence assignment and source-supported NBRC1257/NBRC1321 union. No competing preferred owner of either exact token was found in the explicitly checked current mapped directory and worker01 proposal set, so no owned-name suppression is proposed. These dispositions concern name applicability to this specific preparation, not rejection of bicarbonate as a material. The reported 1.0 M remains nominal: 100 mL is added water, not verified final solution volume; dissolved CO2 amount/speciation is unquantified. Carbon dioxide remains a source-listed material input because the solution is explicitly saturated, independently of the CO2 headspace condition."
        }
      ]
    },
